{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1218164-a-helpful-guide-to-solar-melee","id":1218164,"title":"A Helpful Guide To Solar Melee","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-13T03:30:11-07:00","id":1218164,"title":"A Helpful Guide To Solar Melee","content":"Talking to a friend who was making a Dawn, and having been there myself, I think the size of the charmset is pretty daunting. You get a new charm every 5/8 of a session (probably, unless you are spending your XP on stuff that isn't charms for some reason) so a charmset with over 40 tools to buy is a scary thought. How do you know what you're picking up is actually worth it? For a newer player, or someone who hasn't messed around with solar melee before, it's not overly intuitive which charms you really, really want to have, and which are ultimately not that useful. So this is a guide I wrote up talking about each charm, how important/useful they are to purchase, why I've decided that, and so on. Maybe it can help someone here too, so here it is:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1z2t7aIbxc5PM5GLf9chOefc3FXtPJyhMPC7PUeLKzFA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Melee: So, You've Decided You Want To Win Forever</a><br /> <br /> Critique or pointing out mistakes that should be fixed are much appreciated!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T08:16:56-07:00","id":1218210,"title":"","content":"Genuinely enjoyable and enlightening to read, and I'd like to see more for the other Abilities.<br /> <br /> However, I would prefer if you would give any explanation as to why you deem Glorious Solar Saber a bad choice. I don't feel your recommended house-errata buffs are enough on their own, in this regard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T08:33:34-07:00","id":1218214,"title":"","content":"Great guide with some real solid advice, but I think that Over-and-Under Method is better than you give it credit for. It's a great panic button that allows you to respond to any attack with two of your own, first withering and then decisive, that does not return the Solar to base initiative, allowing it to be used in crash. It's 2m more but that's more than made up for by the fact that it's 1wp less. It's a straight upgrade to what comes before it so I don't see why it shouldn't be at least green, or maybe even blue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2388-nilihum","name":"Nilihum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2388_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T08:53:32-07:00","id":1218226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nilihum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1218164-a-helpful-guide-to-solar-melee?p=1218214#post1218214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great guide with some real solid advice, but I think that Over-and-Under Method is better than you give it credit for. It's a great panic button that allows you to respond to any attack with two of your own, first withering and then decisive, that does not return the Solar to base initiative, allowing it to be used in crash. It's 2m more but that's more than made up for by the fact that it's 1wp less. It's a straight upgrade to what comes before it so I don't see why it shouldn't be at least green, or maybe even blue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can Over and Under really be used in crash? The first attack you roll is a decisive clash, which can't be launched in crash. However, I was rough on it because it requires a second attack roll, but one thing I completely forgot was that this is after they just lost a clash, meaning a -3 defence penalty. So this is a lot better than I first gave it credit for.<br /> <br /> As for other abilities, I haven't personally used Brawl anywhere near as much, so it will be more prone to mistakes, but I could try my hand at one.<br /> <br /> GSS does need more of an explanation, though, so I'll add onto it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T09:25:00-07:00","id":1218230,"title":"","content":"You cannot launch decisive attacks in a crash, even if they don't use your init. The init crash rules clearly say:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A character in Initiative Crash cannot launch decisive attacks. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Some of me humble homebrew for ex3:<br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hOOjEGyoq3owLoUwIwTfWKTffzo_udsiUTwomw7wudA/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Artifacts for Crumple's DB homebrew</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tI2T1Re0G8QOuoXkH7Y4PrKQxk1BPEGpbi82SpkTyIw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Some Lintha QCs</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1O2I_2iWTCflJ36ggkDvjTeXmzFsGHKRxAi6L_Ry6g4w/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A Wyld Behemoth</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8838-tds","name":"TDS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T09:47:32-07:00","id":1218238,"title":"","content":"Really fun to read, and considering my players should exalt next week (yes, the <i>players</i> are exalting, what?) and they're quite obsessed with becoming machines of pure melee death, very useful! Reminds me of color-coded builds and whatnot from D&amp;D btw. Nicely done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T10:04:14-07:00","id":1218242,"title":"","content":"echoing this reminds me of the DND4E styles. It did kind of throw me off since you swapped Purple and Gold but it's still really neat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T10:08:20-07:00","id":1218246,"title":"","content":"Interesting to see the charms broken down. The purple and blue are just a little close for my eyes, but that could be all kinds of just me. Making the charm names in a bigger font size might help a little with that, or maybe a more... magenta-y purple, but it's not exactly a huge issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T10:10:42-07:00","id":1218248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roswynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1218164-a-helpful-guide-to-solar-melee?p=1218238#post1218238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really fun to read, and considering my players should exalt next week (yes, the <i>players</i> are exalting, what?) and they're quite obsessed with becoming machines of pure melee death, very useful! Reminds me of color-coded builds and whatnot from D&amp;D btw. Nicely done.</div> </div> </div> </div>its shamelessly stolen from old dnd guides that used the same colour system. if it aint broke, dont fix it, as they say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T10:26:17-07:00","id":1218255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clownpiece</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1218164-a-helpful-guide-to-solar-melee?p=1218226#post1218226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can Over and Under really be used in crash? The first attack you roll is a decisive clash, which can't be launched in crash. However, I was rough on it because it requires a second attack roll, but one thing I completely forgot was that this is after they just lost a clash, meaning a -3 defence penalty. So this is a lot better than I first gave it credit for.<br /> <br /> As for other abilities, I haven't personally used Brawl anywhere near as much, so it will be more prone to mistakes, but I could try my hand at one.<br /> <br /> GSS does need more of an explanation, though, so I'll add onto it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I read it is that you use Flashing Edge of Dawn first (withering) and then add the result to Fervent Blow. I might be wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2388-nilihum","name":"Nilihum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2388_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T10:30:53-07:00","id":1218259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clownpiece</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1218164-a-helpful-guide-to-solar-melee?p=1218248#post1218248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> its shamelessly stolen from old dnd guides that used the same colour system. if it aint broke, dont fix it, as they say.</div> </div> </div> </div>I knew I had seen it before! I like <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13651-roswynn","name":"Roswynn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T11:29:34-07:00","id":1218280,"title":"","content":"This may have been a bit of a rhetorical question, but I feel a need to answer.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#38761D\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Blazing Solar Bolt</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> [5m 2i 1wp, simple]</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Essence+thresh isn\u2019t the worst damage in the world, but why spend your anima on this?</span></span> </div> </div> </div>You would spend anima on this when you want to hit someone who is very far away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T11:38:07-07:00","id":1218282,"title":"","content":"It's competing with Peony Blossom Strike was more my point, I think I'm overly harsh on Blazing Solar Bolt but it's part of a set of charms that aren't particularly useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T11:51:56-07:00","id":1218288,"title":"","content":"I haven't had time to read much of this yet, but it looks like an interesting and informative read. I have never played a Solar Melee character, so all I have is my impressions to go on for the Charmset, and I'm looking forward to seeing how they compare. Thank you for sharing this.<br /> <br /> One thing, though: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs/page514#post1173406\">According to Vance</a>, Hail-Shattering Practice doesn't work in a clash. It has to enhance a Melee-based Parry attempt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/157-phoenix_kensai","name":"Phoenix_Kensai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar157_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T12:09:59-07:00","id":1218292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clownpiece</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1218164-a-helpful-guide-to-solar-melee?p=1218282#post1218282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's competing with Peony Blossom Strike</div> </div> </div> </div>Not Really. You use Peony Blossom if the enemy is right in front of you, and BSB if he's on the side of a nearby mountain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T12:54:14-07:00","id":1218299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1218164-a-helpful-guide-to-solar-melee?p=1218292#post1218292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not Really. You use Peony Blossom if the enemy is right in front of you, and BSB if he's on the side of a nearby mountain.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're getting into a bit of an overly niche scenario here, since how often do you hit anima 3 with no-one around to fight that isn't really far away? I won't deny it can or has happened, but if its a niche buy I think my placement of it is appropriate.<br /> <br /> As for HSP working on clashes, I don't really agree with the interpretation that it doesn't. There's a few other effects like that too (DED comes to mind), I think clashes might need a proper published ruling explaining what sort of effects are legal to work on them or not. As-is, I can't think of a mechanical reason why HSP or DED would not work on a clash, and if the reason they apparently don't is balance concerns, that seems like something to be properly addressed with errata.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T13:14:06-07:00","id":1218303,"title":"","content":"I honestly don't know why Divine Executioner Stance isn't an Integrity Charm. It's about swearing an oath based on the power of your convictions.<br /> <br /> I never did like Corona of Radiance. I also thought it bad to gate offensive Charms behind a defensive Charm which itself is found behind an attack Charm.<br /> <br /> You should be able to clash ranged attacks with Iron Raptor Technique, and clashing ranged attacks with IRT and SWA could be buffed to project you from the consequences of failing a clash.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T21:04:03-07:00","id":1218398,"title":"","content":"I am <i>really</i> doubtful that you can use Iron Whirlwind Attack, a Simple Charm, on a Reflexive attack created by Peony Blossom Technique (or any other Reflexive attack creator for that matter), and I am absolutely certain that you will not reset to base from Solar Counterattack <i>after</i> your opponent's attack does damage.<br /> <br /> Edit: never mind the first point, I'm dumb, IWA explicitly lets you do so. But resetting to base is still part of resolving an attack, and Solar Counterattack says that the attack occurs between the opponent's attack and damage rolls while providing no text altering when the reset happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":172,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/172-elohteebee","user":"ElOhTeeBee","date":". 05-14-2018, 12:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/172-elohteebee","name":"ElOhTeeBee","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T21:47:16-07:00","id":1218408,"title":"","content":"Edge of Morning Sunlight says that it's Uniform, so it can be used with a Withering or Decisive attack and, if the attack does one level of damage, you roll (essence) damage dice and apply it directly against the opponent's health track, ignoring hardness. That sounds like it's doing direct Decisive Damage even on a Withering attack. Which, ok, it's Creatures of Darkness only, but the upgrade from Sharp Light of Judgement potentially lets you do 1 or 2 HLs of damage with every Withering attack you make against people you really, really hate for 3m.<br /> <br /> Possibly still a bit niche, but it sounds kinda cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T11:15:43-07:00","id":1218621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElOhTeeBee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1218164-a-helpful-guide-to-solar-melee?p=1218398#post1218398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am <i>really</i> doubtful that you can use Iron Whirlwind Attack, a Simple Charm, on a Reflexive attack created by Peony Blossom Technique (or any other Reflexive attack creator for that matter), and I am absolutely certain that you will not reset to base from Solar Counterattack <i>after</i> your opponent's attack does damage.<br /> <br /> Edit: never mind the first point, I'm dumb, IWA explicitly lets you do so. But resetting to base is still part of resolving an attack, and Solar Counterattack says that the attack occurs between the opponent's attack and damage rolls while providing no text altering when the reset happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Solar Counterattack working that way was I believe clarified by Vance, but I can't find the post in question. So maybe I'm wrong. The question of &quot;what the hell happens if you launch solar counterattack against a withering attack&quot; was something no-one had any idea about until the thread, I know that at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T07:34:30-07:00","id":1218908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clownpiece</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1218164-a-helpful-guide-to-solar-melee?p=1218621#post1218621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Solar Counterattack working that way was I believe clarified by Vance, but I can't find the post in question. So maybe I'm wrong. The question of &quot;what the hell happens if you launch solar counterattack against a withering attack&quot; was something no-one had any idea about until the thread, I know that at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, forum search sucks. :/<br /> <br /> I really feel like &quot;Solar Counterattack against withering comes with the risk of getting crashed if your counterattack doesn't straight-up kill your opponent&quot; is healthier for the game than &quot;Solar Counterattack, in addition to destroying action economy for 3m, <i>also</i> serves as a get-out-of-Crash-free card&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/172-elohteebee","name":"ElOhTeeBee","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T08:17:18-07:00","id":1218921,"title":"","content":"Forum search sucks, but you can ctrl-f to your heart's content here, <a href=\"http://www.nishkriya.com/Threads/Details/10319\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.nishkriya.com/Threads/Details/10319</a>.<br /> <br /> I couldn't find anything about resetting after they did damage. I found that even if you kill your attacker, they still get to roll damage- <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1069632#post1069632\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...32#post1069632</a><br /> <br /> I also found a reiteration of the damage timing for the attacker, that if you mistook the attacker in the sentence for the counter-attacker you would come to this interpretation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1071400#post1071400\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...00#post1071400</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T08:24:30-07:00","id":1218925,"title":"","content":"The text of Solar Counterattack is fairly unambiguous: &quot;The Exalt may use this Charm in response to any attack she attempts to parry, creating a Melee counterattack that occurs after the opponent\u2019s attack result, but before damage has been rolled. This attack functions as a regular decisive attack.&quot;<br /> <br /> You create and resolve a regular decisive attack after seeing your opponent's attack result, but before they roll damage. How anybody could interpret this as &quot;you roll attack and damage, but inexplicably <i>don't</i> reset until after they've damaged you, potentially yanking you out of crash without the Charm text explicitly saying so&quot; is beyond me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T08:46:42-07:00","id":1218933,"title":"","content":"So, I asked.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1218920#post1218920\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1218920#post1218920\"> Ask the Devs - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1218920#post1218920\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1218920#post1218920 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Dear Exalted fans, as you may be aware from the latest Onyx Path Monday Meeting notes (http://theonyxpath.com/princes-gambit-joy-exalted-plans-monday-meeting-notes/), Robert Vance and I have been honored with the opportunity to take on line editor duties for Exalted Third Edition. As part of that, we want to make ourselves available to the community as a resource to keep you informed as best we can about the line. Obviously there will be some questions we can't answer! But when we're not working on upcoming books, we'll drop in to touch base. We'll be using this thread as our port of call so that we </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/172-elohteebee","name":"ElOhTeeBee","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T03:15:05-07:00","id":1219218,"title":"","content":"I hate to be a PITA, but could someone make a version of this that doesn't use purple and blue? I'm really colourblind (like, I thought purple existing as a colour was a joke people were playing on me for years), and I can't see the difference <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm happy to do it myself if someone can list the charms that are purple for me. I'll change it to a 5* ranking system so anyone who has another colour-differentiation problems isn't impacted by the change I made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13646-realitycheque","name":"realitycheque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13646_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T03:55:41-07:00","id":1219223,"title":"","content":"Ahhh I didn't consider colourblindness, sorry. The charms that are purple are: Excellent Strike, Fire and Stones Strike, One Weapon Two Blows, Peony Blossom Technique, Dipping Swallow Defence, Solar Counterattack, Iron Whirlwind Attack, Heavenly Guardian Defence, Invincible Fury of the Dawn, Perfect Strike Discipline, Divine Executioner Stance","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T06:48:34-07:00","id":1219258,"title":"","content":"Will you look over Evocations and rate them against Solar Melee Charms?<br /> <br /> For example, the Evocations of All-Conquering Colossus that can be used with Melee attacks and parries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-16T06:52:50-07:00","id":1219259,"title":"","content":"No worries, after 30+ years of playing computer games I'm kinda used to colour vision biting me in the arse ;-)<br /> <br /> Here's the colour tweaked version: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_jcy-SXbPZBUn4XjIKVrm-UbUDx62Q32lrky5k1c9dQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13646-realitycheque","name":"realitycheque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13646_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T07:23:25-07:00","id":1221149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1218164-a-helpful-guide-to-solar-melee?p=1219258#post1219258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will you look over Evocations and rate them against Solar Melee Charms?<br /> <br /> For example, the Evocations of All-Conquering Colossus that can be used with Melee attacks and parries.</div> </div> </div> </div>evocations are a bit awkward, since theyre mutually exclusive and a lot of them rely on specific character types that i cant really rate. some artifacts are plain crazy, too. just imagine &quot;Stormcaller&quot; in 200ft high purple letters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T07:57:43-07:00","id":1221155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clownpiece</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1218164-a-helpful-guide-to-solar-melee?p=1221149#post1221149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">some artifacts are plain crazy, too. just imagine &quot;Stormcaller&quot; in 200ft high purple letters.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd like some explanation for that, because to me, it seems very much like a poster child of &quot;awesome, but impractical&quot; (kinda like Volcano Cutter, but to a lesser extent).<br /> <br /> There are multiple 4-dots (Gnomon, Mistweaver) I'd consider more broadly useful, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T16:09:23-07:00","id":1221293,"title":"","content":"If you were moved to look at Evocations, I\u2019d honestly find a list of which Melee charms work best with which Artifact most helpful. Like, if you grab Gnomon, are you going to want to focus harder on extra attack charms or are you going to want to focus more on hitting harder?<br /> <br /> I could imagine that in most cases it doesn\u2019t matter, but some artifacts might reward different builds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T20:47:19-07:00","id":1221368,"title":"","content":"Any thoughts on how to make the projectile Melee Charms worthwhile?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-23T20:46:39-07:00","id":1221610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1218164-a-helpful-guide-to-solar-melee?p=1221155#post1221155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'd like some explanation for that, because to me, it seems very much like a poster child of &quot;awesome, but impractical&quot; (kinda like Volcano Cutter, but to a lesser extent).<br /> <br /> There are multiple 4-dots (Gnomon, Mistweaver) I'd consider more broadly useful, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>volcano cutter requires, if i remember right from calculating it years ago, 20 rounds or so before you can use its effect. stormcaller can drop an unblockable decisive attack for free at any moment. this isnt the best thing to do with it, though, its more of a fun bonus for after victory. the basic gist is: IFotD is already stupidly strong, and stormcaller lets you crash someone with a cheap double 7s to damage withering attack, then IWA with Hungry Tiger and Sleeping Devil, Wake. That's right, it's supplemental. 5m to add [intensity/2] damage to all attacks and gain 1 intensity for every 10 on your damage rolls. you hit 10 intensity very fast and get to add 5 damage to every IWA hit for 5m total spent, it stacks with fire and stones and isnt as conditional - dont need e5 and 5 thresh to get it. then, just for fun, the next charm upgrades hungry tiger technique so you can skip the crash part and get straight to the slaughter. its a straight, huge upgrade to what is arguably melee's best trick, and arguably the most broken and overpowered charm in the entire combat engine. so yeah. this artifact makes melee supremacy as real as its made out to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T02:55:14-07:00","id":1221639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clownpiece</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1218164-a-helpful-guide-to-solar-melee?p=1221610#post1221610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IFotD is already stupidly strong, and stormcaller lets you crash someone with a cheap double 7s to damage withering attack</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, but you don't actually <i>gain </i>any initiative from that, except for the crash bonus... I mean, yeah, 6 extra initiative is nothing to sneeze at, but it's basically +1 damage die on each of your invincible flurry attacks. You're basically paying 2m 1WP for a benefit that is nearly on par with the 3m version of Increasing Strength Exercise, except the latter is scenelong and doesn't eat up your precious willpower (which you already need for flurries, Perfect Strike Discipline and TAP).<br /> <br /> Which is not to say that the ability to strip a fuckton of initiative off of someone without gaining it <i>isn't </i>without its uses (great way to deal with artifact heavy armor, for example, since it nearly guarantees a crash and therefore shuts down their pesky Hardness; also a good panic button if you know your opponent is going to decisive you next turn and you need to reduce their damage pool ASAP) - but in the overwhelming majority of cases, you're better off just making a regular attack enhanced by FSS if your goal is to load up on initiative (dump 3m into FSS and you'll have a minimum post-soak damage pool of 8, which averages out to 4i, +1 from hitting - the difference between this and FEF is a marginal 1i).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clownpiece</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1218164-a-helpful-guide-to-solar-melee?p=1221610#post1221610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IFotD is already stupidly strong, and stormcaller lets you crash someone with a cheap double 7s to damage withering attack, then IWA with Hungry Tiger and Sleeping Devil, Wake. That's right, it's supplemental. 5m to add [intensity/2] damage to all attacks and gain 1 intensity for every 10 on your damage rolls. you hit 10 intensity very fast</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> See, this is the part where our opinion seems to diverge. I mean - okay, cool, you can Hungry Tiger because they're crashed, awesome; but do you <i>really </i>expect to always have the resources to toss a full excellency on top of every attack? If not, Hungry Tiger honestly isn't much better than FSS in this case, a solid +3 damage on every attack (assuming your opponent has some way to deal with the mounting wound- and onslaught penalties - otherwise, yeah, Hungry Tiger adds up over time). Now, let's say you had an average join battle roll on a 20d pool, putting you at 13 initiative right out of the gate, and you crashed your opponent earlier (19i; let's round up to 20) - now you're gonna make five attacks with 4 (init) +1 (IFoD) +3 (Hungry Tiger) = 8 damage each. Let's also toss an E3 ISE on top of this for another +3 damage, for 11 total (which is starting to strain believability, given that you somehow managed to crash your opponent despite the fact that you've given him at least one free turn to build his initiative while you were powering up). This is a grand total of 55 damage - a very generous assumption, given that it's extremely unlikely that all of your attacks will hit against a peer-level opponent, but let's run with it to balance out that some Hungry Tiger results will produce significantly more than +3 damage. This nets you, on average, +5.5 intensity. Even if we factor in that intensity gained in the middle of the sequence adds even more damage to subsequent attacks, one flurry is extremely unlikely to get you to intensity 10. Intensity 6 on the back of one flurry plus FEF is reasonable.<br /> <br /> Now only one question remains: you just pumped 55 dice of damage into your opponent. To hit intensity 10, you'll need another flurry for similarly ridiculous numbers. <i>What the hell is your built-up intensity gonna be good for, after having dealt over 100 dice of damage already?</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T06:14:58-07:00","id":1221678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1218164-a-helpful-guide-to-solar-melee?p=1221639#post1221639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&lt;hungry tiger stuffs&gt;<br /> Now only one question remains: you just pumped 55 dice of damage into your opponent. To hit intensity 10, you'll need another flurry for similarly ridiculous numbers. <i>What the hell is your built-up intensity gonna be good for, after having dealt over 100 dice of damage already?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>But forcing that intensity up is easier than it looks, to be frank... You have to land decisives at init 15.<br /> Get gangbanged at init 15 with Ready in 8 Directions.<br /> Or IWA at init 15 that's 5 attacks at init 15. SD,W to improve on that.<br /> <br /> Let's look at a dead start iwa+sw,d from a &quot;sword saint&quot;. With a stunt 1 you're throwing 13 dice on your attacks and spent 10m, 2wp.<br /> Against defense 7, that's a hit 48% of the time.<br /> Against 6, 64% hit chance.<br /> Against 5, 79%<br /> Against 4, 90%<br /> Against 3, 96%<br /> <br /> Suppose the enemy is seriously scared of being hit and is pumping his defense to 10 every time and has an onslaught negator like bulwark stance (doesn't get much better than this!).<br /> 5 hits at 11% hit chance either. About a 41% chance to land one hit, and don't expect another. Your opposition spent at least 30m plus the onslaught negators' essence. To maybe get hit once anyway.<br /> <br /> Without an onslaught negator you might as well quit. The 5-hit sequence against defense 12 goes 3%, 6%, 11%, 20%, 33%. Slightly worse off and almost twice as expensive.<br /> <br /> With an excellent strike, since it is so cheap when you are throwing 65 attack dice, those numbers change to...<br /> Against a passive 7er: 75%, 87%, 94%, 98%, 100%<br /> Against a bulwarked 10er: 5 hits at 29% each (83% chance to hit once, 47% to hit twice)<br /> Against a passive 12er: 10%, 18%, 29%, 44%, 60%<br /> <br /> <br /> That dead-start Excellent IWA+SD,W has 4 damage dice per hit (this is the real defense against the cheap combo, hardness means you gotta pay up to land any of this). Against the kind of enemy you can rely on this setup (no bulwark, 3- hardness) you will likely build about 10 intensity on the round.<br /> <br /> From that point onward the excellent iwa+sd,w will work from a baseline of 18 dice, 1 success rather than 13 dice, 1 success. Even a bulwarked 12er is going to get hit a couple times and you just got yourself a nice defensive -3 to all enemy actions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Dueling another sword saint this isn't really viable. Add squishier enemies and suddenly you can get that tasty -3 storm right away, which greatly viabilizes dragging the fight a little and gives you juicier targets for that sheath.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 05-24-2018, 10:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T07:38:00-07:00","id":1221700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1218164-a-helpful-guide-to-solar-melee?p=1221678#post1221678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Against the kind of enemy you can rely on this setup (no bulwark, 3- hardness) you will likely build about 12 intensity on the round.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've got to admit, I can't follow your math on that one. Assuming every single attack in your sequence hits, that's +5 intensity. Where's the other 7 coming from? You'd need, on average, to throw around 70 dice of damage to get there.<br /> <br /> Again, this is my problem: even by getting free intensity increases with every attack, you'd still need to plop down an invincible flurry for 40+ damage on average (1 because you used FEF earlier in the round, 5 from making the attacks while sitting at init 15, need 4 to pump yourself up to max). You just tossed out 40 points of damage! What the hell is still alive and in a decent fighting shape after that?<br /> <br /> (Well, one of my problems. The other is that without hearthstone cheese, you'd need to play for around 30 sessions for this combo to come online. And the other-other one is that while you're showing off your l33t st0rm sk1llz, everybody else at the table silently wishes you would do something else, because they really don't want the -3 penalty on their actions either.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: oh, now I see, it's because you also get intensity from dealing damage with SDW.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":". 05-24-2018, 10:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T07:58:35-07:00","id":1221710,"title":"","content":"Four hits out of five, 16 damage dice over the hits gives you 1-2 more from rolled 10s, 4 damage dice have a 90% chance to deal any damage, averaging some 3-4 more.<br /> <br /> Without any damage booster, an easy target will give you anywhere from 4 to 10 dice, more if you're lucky (4 is if you really deal no damage). I'll correct it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T08:20:18-07:00","id":1221714,"title":"","content":"Oh, and I agree with you, on a duel it's probably going to be overkill. Stormcaller's kit is best suited to fight multiple enemies, preferably over long fights.<br /> <br /> Against single targets you basically have that fulminating edge flash if you really just <b>need</b> to drop your foe's initiative and drive it into crash, and later Divine Tempest Blade.<br /> <br /> So for single target you're basically looking at an easy way to crash the enemy to either get straight into murdering it or dragging the fight along.<br /> It's a very dramatic way to drag the fight, great for those struggles where you two are clashing for some reason that maybe just maybe can be talked over!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T09:57:10-07:00","id":1221742,"title":"","content":"Volcano Cutter's purpose, if I remember right, was destroying behemoths. Long, prolonged, <i>God of War</i> spectacle-boss fights which could conceivably last 20 rounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T10:11:01-07:00","id":1222455,"title":"","content":"Every night I pray to whatever dark gods can hear me that I am never in a 20 round Exalted combat.<br /> <br /> I love the engine truly and deeply but after 5 or 6 rounds characters are running on empty and things start to turn into a slog. Thankfully, it's very rare for a fight to even last past those 5 or 6 rounds in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Clownpiece","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12762_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T11:04:49-07:00","id":1222468,"title":"","content":"So, do you think Volcano Cutter needs a buff? Or are the heights of its power simply too high?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T14:06:41-07:00","id":1222503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clownpiece</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1218164-a-helpful-guide-to-solar-melee?p=1222455#post1222455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every night I pray to whatever dark gods can hear me that I am never in a 20 round Exalted combat.<br /> <br /> I love the engine truly and deeply but after 5 or 6 rounds characters are running on empty and things start to turn into a slog. Thankfully, it's very rare for a fight to even last past those 5 or 6 rounds in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Especially Solar combat. Things are just too nuclear for a combat to last 20 rounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T04:43:39-07:00","id":1222612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1218164-a-helpful-guide-to-solar-melee?p=1222468#post1222468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, do you think Volcano Cutter needs a buff? Or are the heights of its power simply too high?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it needs to be remade fundamentally, and I welcome someone to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12762-clownpiece","name":"Cl